      "title": "[tygodnik-rolniczy.pl] Poland lifts ASF restrictions in 254 municipalities, eases them in 63",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://kagiproxy.com/img/BcXXgnAs0BExCYQoQKFih7_VCv1yS2eC0bGEAAp-wXxW1hewXXlQRMCMVkaNc6eHC853SUhP6sPEuaQu5ZSFtXOa6zpnIE6L1-1mWa9tZEcfmfKZX9k3Rj0\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\nPoland lifted African swine fever (ASF) restrictions in 254 municipalities and eased them in 63 others effective Nov. 26, under a European Commission regulation published the previous day. The changes affect eight provinces and reduce restrictions on the movement of pigs, pork and pork products.\n\nPig prices remain low, and production costs at some farms exceed their returns. The agriculture ministry says it will continue removing restrictions where animal-health conditions allow.",
      "date_published": "2026-11-26T15:30:00+00:00",
      "authors": [
