    {
      "id": "https://gazetadeagricultura.info/ansvsa/romania-semneaza-certificatele-sanitar-veterinare-cu-iordania",
      "url": "https://gazetadeagricultura.info/ansvsa/romania-semneaza-certificatele-sanitar-veterinare-cu-iordania",
      "title": "[gazetadeagricultura.info] Romania signs sheep export certificates, but restrictions still block trade",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://gazetadeagricultura.info/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ANSVSA_semnare_cert_xn1300.webp\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\nRomania’s National Veterinary and Food Safety Authority and Jordan signed health certificates on Nov. 25 for exports of live sheep and sheep carcasses, setting conditions for entry into Jordan’s market. The certificates do not lift the restrictions blocking shipments; exports can resume only after those restrictions are lifted, and no restart date was announced.\n\nThe agreement followed visits by Jordanian officials to farms and processing businesses in Constanța and Tulcea, where they assessed biosecurity, processing and veterinary controls. The Romanian authority said vaccination of sheep and goats supports, rather than blocks, export access.",
