      "title": "[Larry Coble] Beekeeping Vocabulary – “W” is for…",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://i0.wp.com/beekeeping365.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/12/beeswax-5.jpg?fit=635%2C265&amp;ssl=1\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\nBeeswax is a natural substance produced by worker honey bees to build honeycomb and protect developing brood. Mainly composed of fatty acid esters, it melts at 62–64°C and softens with warmth. Although nutritionally insignificant, beeswax is food-approved and widely used in cosmetics, pharmaceuticals, candles, polishes, adhesives, crafts, and surgical products.",
